I just had one of the closest escapes I've ever had, and I'm not out of
the woods yet...

Long story short: I'd killed Rodney, taken the Book, and headed down to
the previously-located vibrating square, where I discovered that I
didn't have the Bell of Opening on me.  I eventually found it in a stash
on level 21, having had to kill Rodney a couple of times along the way.
(I took a months-long break in the game, long enough for me to forget
some important details like that.)  The stash was so well-stocked that I
took some time to kit myself out as well as possible.  Rodney showed up
again at one point, but I took him out at once with a death ray.  A
little later, when I realized that I'd been wearing a +3 cloak of MR
over GDSM, I thought I'd be better off enchanting a +0 cloak of
protection from the stash.  I removed all of my armor, put on the
cloak...and Rodney chose that precise moment to reappear, much sooner
that I would have thought possible.  Eep!

I squeezed off another death ray and missed.  Another ray, another
miss.  Rodney cast a spell and I lost over half my hit points.
Unfortunately, I fat-fingered the ID command trying to determine which @
in the room was Rodney (the other being a priest), and accidentally used
up an action hitting him bare-handed.  D'oh!  I let off yet another
death ray and missed again.  Rodney summoned nasties.

Having no other real option, I risked teleporting to the upstairs
(thanks to a scroll and a ring of TC), frantically climbed, and was
alone for the moment.  I dug a potion of full healing out of my BoH and
healed back up.  Now I'm trying to figure out how best to use my limited
time until Rodney finds me.

#1 priority of course is to get my magic resistance back.  I don't know
if I have enough time to put on my GDSM.  I have a scroll of earth in my
bag and thought about building a fort, but I'm not sure how much
protection that would afford.  Presumably it would keep away the dreaded
touch of death, but at what range can Rodney hit me with that
heavy-damage spell?  Even two of them could do me in if he could get
them off while I'm squeezing into my armor.  (And actually, how much
does MR reduce the damage from that spell anyway?)

I have a wand of wishing with two charges in hand; I've considered
wishing for another cloak of magic resistance (I regrettably cast away
the original one that I mentioned above), which I assume I could put on
faster, but I'm not really sure.

Any other suggestions?  How much more time do I probably have before
Rodney reappears, anyway?


